 160:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * Function Name: CySysPmHibernate
 161:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     ****************************************************************************//**
 162:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     *
 163:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * Puts the part into the Hibernate state. Only SRAM and UDBs are retained;
 164:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * most internal supplies are off. Wakeup is possible from a pin or a hibernate
 165:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * comparator only.
 166:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     *
 167:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * It is expected that the firmware has already frozen the IO-Cells using
 168:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * CySysPmFreezeIo() function before the call to this function. If this is
 169:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * omitted, the IO-cells will be frozen in the same way as they are
 170:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * in the Active to Deep Sleep transition, but will lose their state on wake up
 171:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * (because of the reset occurring at that time).
 172:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     *
 173:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * Because all the CPU state is lost, the CPU will start up at the reset vector.
 174:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * To save the firmware state through the Hibernate low power mode, a
 175:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * corresponding variable should be defined with CY_NOINIT attribute. It
ARM GAS  C:\Users\taips\AppData\Local\Temp\cc1AWS9X.s 			page 7


 176:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * prevents data from being initialized to zero on startup. The interrupt
 177:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * cause of the hibernate peripheral is retained, such that it can be either
 178:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * read by the firmware or cause an interrupt after the firmware has booted and
 179:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * enabled the corresponding interrupt. To distinguish the wakeup from
 180:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * the Hibernate mode and the general Reset event, the
 181:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * \ref CySysPmGetResetReason() function could be used.
 182:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     *
 183:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     *******************************************************************************/
