 224:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     *
 225:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * Puts the part into the Stop state. All internal supplies are off;
 226:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * no state is retained.
 227:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     *
 228:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * Wakeup from Stop is performed by toggling the wakeup pin, causing
 229:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * a normal boot procedure to occur. To configure the wakeup pin,
 230:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * the Digital Input Pin component should be placed on the schematic,
 231:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * assigned to the wakeup pin, and resistively pulled up or down to the inverse
 232:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * state of the wakeup polarity. To distinguish the wakeup from the Stop mode
 233:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * and the general Reset event, \ref CySysPmGetResetReason() function could be
 234:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * used.  The wakeup pin is active low by default. The wakeup pin polarity
 235:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * could be changed with the \ref CySysPmSetWakeupPolarity() function.
 236:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     *
 237:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * This function freezes IO cells implicitly. It is not possible to enter
