 394:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * The IO-Cells remain frozen after awake from Hibernate or Stop mode until
 395:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * the firmware unfreezes them after booting. The call of this function
 396:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * unfreezes IO-Cells explicitly.
 397:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     *
 398:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * If the firmware intent is to retain the data value on the port, then the
 399:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * value must be read and re-written to the data register before calling this
 400:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * API. Furthermore, the drive mode must be re-programmed.  If this is not done,
 401:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO4.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cyPm.c ****     * the pin state will change to default state the moment the freeze is removed.
